    "result_text": "All green \u2014 build succeeds and the acceptance test passes. The audit log confirms the unified id: `memberId=NSW2616E6609E3` (`NSW` region + `26` fiscal year + `16E6609E` HASH8 + `3` Luhn check).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**New behaviour in one small, cohesive unit** \u2014 `util/MemberIds.java` (new): `build`/`buildUnique` compose `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (reusing `Localities`, `FiscalYears`, `CheckDigits`), plus `regionOf` (leading-letter run) and `fiscalYearLabel` readers. Deleted `util/CustomerCodes.java`, which it replaces.\n\n**Minimal touches to the large classes** (to keep `WMC_other` cost down):\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 field `customerCode`\u2192`memberId`; renamed the two accessor/assign methods; `assignMemberId` now also passes `registrationDate`.\n- `service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` \u2014 the single `saveOwner` guard/assign call switched to `getMemberId`/`assignMemberId`.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 `memberId` mapping replaces `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit`; `locality`/`ownerSegment`/`timezone` now read the region from `memberId`; `fiscalYear` derives from `memberId`; removed the `membershipNumber()` method.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 audit line logs `memberId` (dropped `membershipNumber`).\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 DTO now has `memberId`; removed `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`.\n\n**Left untouched deliberately:** the DB column stays `customer_code` (Owner just maps `memberId` onto it), avoiding schema/seed-data edits; and `OwnerCreatedEvent` is already identifier-agnostic by design (its doc calls out \"a unified memberId\"), so the controller simply passes the memberId to it \u2014 no file change needed there.\n\nOne honest note: `OwnerCreatedEvent`'s JSON still uses the key `\"customerCode\"` for that agnostic identifier slot (now carrying the memberId value). No test or spec clause pins that key name, and changing it would touch an otherwise-unaffected file, so I left it. Say the word if you'd like the key renamed to `memberId` for clarity.",
